---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/v02.css';
import V02DatasetPicker from '../components/V02DatasetPicker.astro';
import {jsonFile,reviews,dataDir,ROOT} from '../lib/v02-store';
import path from 'node:path';
import fs from 'node:fs';
export const prerender=false;
const selected=path.basename(dataDir(Astro.url.searchParams.get('dataset')));
const dataset=jsonFile('review.json',{turns:[],status:{completed:0,total:0}},selected);
const latest=reviews(selected);
let prefix=0;for(const t of dataset.turns){if(!(t.has_prediction??!!t.prediction)||!['approved','corrected'].includes(latest[t.id]?.status))break;prefix++;}
const lastExport=jsonFile('training/manifest.json',null,selected);
const machineExport=jsonFile('training/machine_teacher/manifest.json',null,selected);
// LoRA jobs that ran (cards file written from the master relay; same source as the eval page).
let jobs:any[]=[];try{jobs=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT,'data/v02/_eval/training-cards.json'),'utf8')).filter((c:any)=>c.state==='done');}catch{}
---
<Layout title="V0.2 · Training readiness"><main class="v02">
<header class="masthead"><div><p class="eyebrow">CCT SUMMARIZER / V0.2</p><h1>Build the reference before training.</h1><p>Local data preparation is ready. No paid API or training jobs run from this dashboard.</p></div><nav class="links"><a href="/review">Review predictions →</a><a href="/training-v01">V0.1 archive</a></nav></header>
    <V02DatasetPicker />
<div class="eval-grid"><article class="panel stat"><small>Generated draft turns</small><div class="value">{dataset.status.completed} / {dataset.status.total}</div><p class="muted">{dataset.manifest?.window_start_iso} → {dataset.manifest?.window_end_iso} · {dataset.status.state}</p></article><article class="panel stat"><small>Contiguous reviewed turns</small><div class="value">{prefix}</div><p class="muted">Export stops at the first unreviewed or rejected turn so earlier state stays trustworthy.</p></article><article class="panel stat"><small>Training jobs run</small><div class="value">{jobs.length}</div><p class="muted">{jobs.length ? `LoRA on ${jobs[0].provider}, launched outside this dashboard` : "None on record."}</p></article></div>
{jobs.length>0 && <section class="panel stat" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>LoRA training jobs</h2><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px"><thead><tr><th align="left">version</th><th align="left">base</th><th align="left">provider</th><th align="right">minutes</th><th align="right">rows</th><th align="right">epochs</th><th align="right">rank</th><th align="right">train / val loss</th><th align="left">served as</th></tr></thead><tbody>{jobs.map((j:any,i:number)=><tr><td>{j.version}{jobs.length-1>i?" (superseded)":""}</td><td>{String(j.base).split("/").pop()}</td><td>{j.provider}</td><td align="right">~{j.minutes}</td><td align="right">{j.train_rows}</td><td align="right">{j.epochs}</td><td align="right">{j.rank}</td><td align="right">{j.train_loss} / {j.val_loss}</td><td>{j.served_as}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="muted">Teachers: {jobs.map((j:any)=>`${j.version}: ${j.teachers}`).join(" · ")}. Eval results: <a href="/eval">eval page</a>.</p></section>}
<section class="panel stat" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>Human-reviewed export</h2><p class="muted">Day 1 is the machine teacher baseline. Machine-label export is available below; rollout evaluation is being prepared separately. The existing reviewed export requires human-reviewed turns.</p><p style="margin:12px 0">Review turns in order, starting with <a href="/review?turn=turn-0001">turn #1</a>. The exporter replays your corrections, builds causal context, then splits chronologically with a two-turn gap. At least ten reviewed turns are required to prepare a train/validation split; that is a tooling threshold, not evidence of sufficient training data.</p><pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere">CCT_V02_DATASET={selected} python3 scripts/v02/export_training.py</pre><p class="muted">Run from the V0.2 worktree. Files stay under data/v02/{selected}/training/. Nothing is uploaded.</p><p style="margin-top:12px">Last export: {lastExport?.reviewed_contiguous_prefix??0} reviewed turns, {lastExport?.train_examples??0} training examples, {lastExport?.validation_examples??0} validation examples.</p><p class="footer-note">Corrections preserve the original machine labels. If changing an entity invalidates references in later turns, the exporter stops for correction instead of silently changing identity.</p></section>
<section class="panel stat" style="margin-top:20px"><h2>Machine teacher baseline export</h2><p style="margin:12px 0">The designated Luna Day 1 baseline can train a model to imitate its labels. This is separate from human gold. The exporter preserves the recorded input and original prediction, freezes hashes, and creates a temporal split with a two-turn gap. It requires completed Day 1 by default.</p><pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere">CCT_V02_DATASET=day1 python3 scripts/v02/export_machine_teacher.py</pre><p class="muted">Incomplete previews require --allow-incomplete-prefix. No inference, upload or training job is launched. A temporal split inside one Gamejam does not measure cross-project generalization.</p><p style="margin-top:12px">Selected run's latest export: {machineExport ? `${machineExport.accepted_pairs} pairs · ${machineExport.train_examples} train / ${machineExport.validation_examples} validation · ${machineExport.preview_mode?'incomplete preview':'complete source window'}` : 'No machine teacher export for this run.'}</p></section>
</main></Layout>
